\f0\fs24 \cf2 Take a look at this capital: its shape is anything but random, it\'92s inspired by a very specific source. The Bagatti Valsecchi brothers drew from a 
\f1\i peduccio
\f0\i0  in the Ducal Palace of Urbino, a decorative element featuring an anthropomorphic flower flanked by strange, monstrous little creatures.\
But in the preparatory drawing, done in black ink on graph paper, something shifts. The vegetal garlands disappear, and the monstrous figures give way to more abstract motifs. It\'92s a simplification, yes, but one that doesn\'92t weaken the design, which remains remarkably faithful to the original.\
This small capital reveals a lot about the brothers\'92 method: starting from a photograph, moving to a reinterpretation on paper, and finally entrusting it to the skilled hands of artisans. Every element is the product of a collaborative process, where past and present are in constant dialogue.\
And here\'92s one last clue for keen-eyed visitors: you\'92ll find the same capital in the library. Will you recognize it?}